# Copy to .env for local development.  .env is gitignored.
#
# NOTHING SECRET LIVES HERE.
# Entra public clients have no client secret by design, and the client id is
# visible in the sign-in URL anyway. This file exists so you do not have to
# export a variable in every shell.
#
# Not needed to try the app: `npm run app` -> "Preview with sample data" works
# with this file absent. See TESTING.md.

# --- Desktop app: Microsoft sign-in ----------------------------------------
# The multi-tenant Entra application id, inlined into the bundle at BUILD time
# by scripts/build-app.mjs. Register it once: DISTRIBUTION.md section 1.
# Without it the app runs, shows a "not configured" banner, and disables
# Microsoft sign-in. Google is unaffected — its client id is entered in the UI.
SECURIX_ENTRA_CLIENT_ID=

# --- CLI only ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The CLI uses your OWN single-tenant registration, not the SecuriX app.
# Read with: node --env-file=.env dist/index.js
AZURE_TENANT_ID=
AZURE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- Debugging --------------------------------------------------------------
# AI_AUDIT_LENS_DEBUG=1
# HTTPS_PROXY=http://127.0.0.1:8080
# NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS=/path/to/corp-root.pem
